-- title:
--   Proof of Theorem 6.1, p.35 — $\operatorname{Tr}_R(U_C) = T$
-- statement:
--   Let $U_C$ be the operator (6.4) and $T$ the matrix (6.3). For every $y\in\{0,1\}^n$,
--   $$\big(\operatorname{Tr}_R(U_C)\big)|y\rangle = \sum_{x}\big(\langle x|\otimes I_Q\big)U_C\big(|x\rangle\otimes|y\rangle\big) = \sum_{x}\langle x|U(x)|y\rangle\,|x\rangle = T|y\rangle.$$
--
--   Combined with Lemma 4.1 this identifies the unitary generated by the pure PMG of Theorem 6.1 with $T$.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - generalization: unitary U_{i,a}, h with (6.2) → arbitrary single-qubit operators U_{i,a} and any h; reason: the computation uses neither hypothesis; the paper's setting is a special case
--   - generalization: n ∈ ℕ (positive integers; the paper writes ℕ ∪ {0} when 0 is allowed, p.19) → n : ℕ, including n = 0; reason: the n = 0 instance is true (a single vertex, trivial registers); every positive n is an instance
-- source:
--   Shmueli, What Can Be Computed with Indefinite Causal Structure?, arXiv:2610.40573 (version of 2026-11-03, sha256 d3e36399…b606), proof of Theorem 6.1, 'The generated channel', p.35 (PDF p.37)

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_ICSCompute_Tmat

namespace ICSCompute

open QAlgorithms

/-- **`Tr_R(U_C) = T`** (Shmueli, *What Can Be Computed with Indefinite Causal Structure?*,
arXiv:2610.40573, version of 2026-11-03, sha256 d3e36399…b606, proof of Theorem 6.1, "The
generated channel", p.35 (PDF p.37)): for every `y ∈ {0,1}ⁿ`,
`(Tr_R(U_C))|y⟩ = ∑_x (⟨x| ⊗ I_Q) U_C (|x⟩ ⊗ |y⟩) = ∑_x ⟨x|U(x)|y⟩ |x⟩ = T|y⟩`.

**Formalization Note** `U_C` is the matrix (6.4) (`UCmat`, register `R` first), `T` is (6.3)
(`Tmat`). The chain holds for arbitrary single-qubit operators `U_{i,a}` and any `h`, so no
unitarity or (6.2) hypothesis is stated. `(⟨x| ⊗ I_Q) U_C (|x⟩ ⊗ |y⟩)` is the vector
`q ↦ U_C((x, q), (x, y))` and `⟨x|U(x)|y⟩` is the entry `U(x)_{x,y}`. -/
theorem ptrace_uc_eq_T {n : ℕ} (U : Fin n → Bool → Matrix Bool Bool ℂ) (h : Qubits n → Qubits n)
    (y : Qubits n) :
    Matrix.mulVec (ptraceR (UCmat U h)) (Pi.single y 1) = ∑ x : Qubits n, (fun q => UCmat U h (x, q) (x, y)) ∧
      ∑ x : Qubits n, (fun q => UCmat U h (x, q) (x, y)) =
        ∑ x : Qubits n, Ux U h x x y • (Pi.single x 1 : Qubits n → ℂ) ∧
      ∑ x : Qubits n, Ux U h x x y • (Pi.single x 1 : Qubits n → ℂ) = Matrix.mulVec (Tmat U h) (Pi.single y 1) := by sorry

end ICSCompute
